1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,275
Adding a reranker is another model call.

2
00:00:03,575 --> 00:00:06,300
It can still make your RAG system cheaper.

3
00:00:07,317 --> 00:00:14,992
A self-hosted reranker on one GPU costs about
0.6 to 3 cents per 1,000 queries.

4
00:00:15,617 --> 00:00:21,056
But if it lets you send 8 chunks instead of
20, that's about 6,000 fewer input

5
00:00:21,056 --> 00:00:22,242
tokens per query.

6
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:29,486
At an illustrative $1 per million input
tokens, that saves about $6 per 1,000

7
00:00:29,486 --> 00:00:30,175
queries.

8
00:00:31,183 --> 00:00:36,737
So count the reranker's net cost: what it
costs, minus the generation tokens it

9
00:00:36,737 --> 00:00:37,158
saves.

10
00:00:38,183 --> 00:00:40,808
The full article is on vidyal.ai.
